<title>TUNISIA: Tunisian treasury raises 33 million dinars at auction.</title>
<headline>Tunisian treasury raises 33 million dinars at auction.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tunisian Treasury on Tuesday said it sold 33 million dinars of 13-,26-, 52-week bills and two-year notes at its weekly auction on January 7, repaying maturing paper totalling 21.2 million dinars.</p>
<p>The issue raised the following amounts, in million dinars:</p>
<p>   maturity	 amount	 coupon rate</p>
<p>  -13-week bill     4.0		 7.8125</p>
<p>  -26-week bill     18.0		7.8750</p>
<p>  -52-week bill     10.0		7.8750</p>
<p>   -Two-year notes   1.0		7.9375</p>
<p>Banks bid for 475 million dinars of 13-, 26-, 52-week and two-, three-, four-, five-, ten-, 15-year paper at between 7.8125 and 12.5 percent.</p>
<p>($=one dinar)</p>
<p>--Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
